#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Graph access is granted directly by a graph permission in every mode. Permissive also grants access when the user has permission for the graph's device or template. Restrictive requires permission for both the device and template when there is no direct graph permission. Device Based requires device permission, and Graph Template Based requires template permission. User and group policies are evaluated separately and their allowed results are combined. These modes trade query performance against fine-grained permissions on large installations."
msgstr "Direktang ibinibigay ang access sa graph sa pamamagitan ng graph permission sa bawat mode. Ang Permissive ay nagbibigay rin ng access kapag may permission ang user para sa device o template ng graph. Ang Restrictive ay nangangailangan ng permission para sa parehong device at template kapag walang direktang graph permission. Ang Device Based ay nangangailangan ng device permission, at ang Graph Template Based ay nangangailangan ng template permission. Hiwalay na sinusuri ang mga patakaran ng user at group at pinagsasama ang kanilang mga pinahihintulutang resulta. Ipinagpapalit ng mga mode na ito ang query performance laban sa mas pinong mga permission sa malalaking installation."

#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Permissive"
msgstr "Maluwag"

#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Restrictive"
msgstr "Mahigpit"

#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Device Based"
msgstr "Batay sa Device"

#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Graph/Data Source Creation Method"
msgstr "Paraan ng Paglikha ng Graph/Data Source"

#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "If set to Simple, Graphs and Data Sources can only be created from New Graphs.  If Advanced, legacy Graph and Data Source creation is supported."
msgstr "Kung nakatakda sa Simple, ang mga Graph at Data Source ay malilikha lamang mula sa New Graphs.  Kung Advanced, suportado ang legacy na paglikha ng Graph at Data Source."

#: include/global_settings.php
